<setup>
    <selectFromSequence name="a" from="-1" to="1" step="2"/>
    <selectFromSequence name="b" from="-2" to="2" step="2"/>
    <selectFromSequence name="c" from="-2" to="2" step="2" exclude="$b -1*($b)"/>

    <function symbolic="false" name="f">$a*x + $b*sin(x) + $c*cos(x)</function>
    <derivative name="fP">$f</derivative>
    <derivative name="fPP">$fP</derivative>
</setup>

<p>
  Let <m>f(x) = <math simplify>$f</math></m>.
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>Determine the following derivative formulas: </p>
      <p>
        <answer>
          <label><m>f'(x)=</m></label> 
          $fP
        </answer>
      </p>
      <p><m>f''(x)=</m><answer>$fPP</answer></p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Determine an exact value of <m>x</m> such that <m>f'(x)=0</m> and <m>0 \lt x \lt 2\pi</m>.  If there are no such values, enter <q>none</q>.  Be sure to use the unit circle to find the exact angle value of <m>x</m> that makes the derivative zero.
      </p>

      <p>
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.00000001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
          <mathInput name="crnum">
            <label>
              <m>x = </m>
            </label>
          </mathInput>
          <award matchPartial>
            <when>
              (0 < $crnum < 2*pi) and $$fP($crnum) = 0
            </when>
          </award>
        </answer>
      </p>
      <feedback condition="(0 > $crnum or $crnum > 2*pi)">
        Make sure you are entering an answer that lies betweeen <m>0</m> and <m>2\pi</m>.
      </feedback>
      <feedback condition="0.00000001 < |$$fP($crnum)| < 5">
        Make sure you are entering your answer exactly in radians, entered as a fraction times <m>\pi</m> or whole number times <m>\pi</m>.
      </feedback>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>Determine an exact value of <m>x</m> such that <m>0 \lt x \lt 2\pi</m> and <m>f''(x)</m> changes sign at that <m>x</m>-value.  If there are no such values, enter <q>none</q>. </p>
      <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.00000001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
          <mathInput name="poi">
            <label>
              <m>x = </m>
            </label>
          </mathInput>
          <award matchPartial>
            <when>
              (0 < $poi< 2*pi) and $$fPP($poi) = 0
            </when>
          </award>
        </answer>
      <feedback condition="0.00000001 < |$$fPP($poi)| < 5">
        Make sure you are entering your answer exactly in radians, entered as a fraction times <m>\pi</m> or whole number times <m>\pi</m>.
      </feedback>
    </li>

  </ol>
</p>